[HEADING=1]Privacy policy[/HEADING]

This policy is placeholder text for a demo forum. It lists the kind of information a community site typically handles.

[HEADING=2]What is collected[/HEADING]

[LIST]
[*][B]Account details[/B]: username, email address and the profile fields you choose to fill in.
[*][B]Content[/B]: threads, posts, profile messages and conversations you write.
[*][B]Technical data[/B]: browser and operating system, shown next to your posts and in your list of devices.
[/LIST]

[HEADING=2]How it is used[/HEADING]

The information is used to run the forum: to show your content, to keep your account secure and to prevent abuse. It is not sold.

[HEADING=2]Cookies[/HEADING]

A single cookie keeps you signed in. No advertising or tracking cookies are set.

[HEADING=2]Your choices[/HEADING]

You can edit your profile at any time from your [URL=/account]account[/URL]. To have your account and personal data removed, use the [URL=/contact]contact page[/URL].

[HEADING=2]Retention[/HEADING]

Posts stay visible after an account is closed unless their removal is requested. Technical data is kept only as long as it is needed.
